insert into passages (id, kind, title, body, script) values
  ('R1', 'reading', 'The Saguaro Cactus', '["The saguaro cactus, which grows only in the Sonoran Desert of the southwestern United States and northern Mexico, is among the slowest-growing plants in North America. A saguaro may take ten years to reach a height of merely one inch, and it does not produce its first branch, or arm, until it is roughly seventy years old. Yet a mature specimen can exceed forty feet and weigh several tons, most of that weight being stored water.","The plant''s survival depends on an unusually shallow but extensive root system. Rather than sending a taproot deep underground, the saguaro spreads a dense mat of roots only three inches below the surface, radiating outward as far as the plant is tall. This arrangement allows it to absorb enormous quantities of water within hours of a rainfall. The stem, pleated like an accordion, then expands to accommodate the intake and contracts slowly during the months of drought that follow.","Saguaros are also central to the desert''s animal life. Gila woodpeckers and gilded flickers excavate nesting cavities in the trunk; the cactus responds by forming hard callus tissue around the wound, creating a durable chamber that later shelters owls, flycatchers, and bats long after the original occupants have gone. In early summer the white flowers open at night and close by the following afternoon, a schedule that favors bats as pollinators, though bees and white-winged doves visit them during the brief morning hours.","Despite this resilience, the species is vulnerable. Seedlings require the shade of a nurse plant, typically a paloverde or mesquite, to survive their first decades, and the gradual loss of these companion trees to grazing and development has thinned saguaro regeneration across much of its range."]', null),
  ('R2', 'reading', 'Railroads and Standard Time', '["Before 1883, time in the United States was a local affair. Each town set its clocks by the sun, so that noon in one city might fall several minutes earlier or later than noon in a town fifty miles away. As long as travel moved at the pace of a horse, the discrepancies were harmless. The railroad made them intolerable.","By the 1870s the country was crossed by hundreds of rail lines, each keeping its own standard, usually the local time of its headquarters city. A traveler changing trains in Pittsburgh had to reconcile as many as six different timetables, and station clocks in some depots displayed three or four dials at once. More seriously, the confusion produced collisions: two trains sharing a single track depended on schedules that assumed a common notion of the hour.","The solution came not from Congress but from the railroads themselves. In October 1883 the General Time Convention, an association of railway managers, agreed to divide the continent into four zones, each an hour apart, with boundaries drawn where major lines met. On November 18, remembered afterward as the day of two noons, cities across the country reset their clocks. Some resisted; a few municipalities kept local time for years, and the arrangement received no federal recognition until the Standard Time Act of 1918.","The episode is often cited as an early instance of private industry establishing a public standard. The railroads had no authority to compel anyone, yet within a decade their zones governed schools, courts, and factories. Convenience, not legislation, did the work."]', null),
  ('R3', 'reading', 'Light in the Deep Ocean', '["More than three-quarters of the animals living below two hundred meters in the open ocean produce their own light. The chemistry involved is remarkably uniform: a molecule called luciferin is oxidized in the presence of an enzyme, luciferase, releasing energy almost entirely as light rather than heat. The efficiency is extraordinary. Close to ninety-five percent of the energy becomes visible light, compared with roughly ten percent for an incandescent bulb.","What varies is purpose. For the anglerfish, a luminous lure suspended above the mouth draws prey close enough to be seized. For the hatchetfish, rows of light organs along the belly perform the opposite function, matching the faint glow filtering down from the surface so that predators below see no silhouette, a tactic known as counterillumination. Some squid eject clouds of luminous fluid, a bright equivalent of ink, and escape while the attacker is dazzled.","Most oceanic bioluminescence is blue-green, a consequence of physics rather than preference: seawater transmits those wavelengths farthest, and the eyes of deep-sea animals have narrowed accordingly, sensitive to a band only a few tens of nanometers wide. A few species exploit that narrowness. The dragonfish emits red light, invisible to nearly every other animal in its habitat, and uses it as a private searchlight to inspect prey that cannot detect the beam.","Not all of the light is the animal''s own. Many fishes and squid cultivate colonies of luminous bacteria in specialized pouches, feeding them nutrients in exchange for illumination that the host can shutter with a fold of tissue or rotate out of view."]', null),
  ('R4', 'reading', 'The Harlem Renaissance', '["Between the end of the First World War and the middle of the 1930s, the neighborhood of Harlem in upper Manhattan became the center of an extraordinary concentration of African American writing, music, and visual art. The movement had no manifesto and no single leader, and its participants disagreed sharply about what it was for. Yet it is conventionally treated as a coherent period, the Harlem Renaissance.","Its immediate cause was demographic. The Great Migration brought roughly one and a half million people north between 1916 and 1930, drawn by wartime industrial jobs and pushed by the collapse of southern agriculture. Harlem, built for a white middle class that never fully arrived, had housing available, and it absorbed a population dense enough to sustain its own newspapers, theaters, and publishing outlets.","The writers who emerged there worked in no common style. Countee Cullen preferred the traditional forms of English verse. Langston Hughes built his lines on the rhythms of blues and jazz and was criticized by some contemporaries for depicting working-class life too plainly. Zora Neale Hurston, trained as an anthropologist, drew on folklore she had collected in Florida and the Caribbean.","The debate running beneath the period concerned audience. Much of the movement''s financial support came from white patrons and publishers, and several writers questioned whether work produced under such conditions could represent the community honestly. The Depression ended the patronage and much of the publishing, but the argument about who art is made for outlasted the movement that raised it."]', null),
  ('LB1', 'listening', 'Part B — Percakapan di perpustakaan', null, '[["W","Excuse me. I''m looking for a book called Coastal Erosion in the Great Lakes, but the catalog says the library doesn''t own it."],["M","That''s right. You can request it through interlibrary loan, though. We borrow from about forty other campuses."],["W","How long does that usually take?"],["M","For a book, seven to ten days. Articles are faster; those normally arrive as scans within two days."],["W","That might be too late. My research proposal is due in a week."],["M","Then let me suggest something else. The regional depository downtown keeps a copy on the open shelf. If you go in person with your student ID, you can check it out the same day. It''s about twenty minutes on the number nine bus."],["W","Is there any cost for interlibrary loan, in case I need it later?"],["M","No charge for students. There is a late fee, though — three dollars a day, because the lending library sets those terms, not us."],["W","I''ll try the depository first, then. Thank you."]]'),
  ('LC1', 'listening', 'Part C — Ceramah biologi', null, '[["M","Today I want to finish our unit on animal navigation with the monarch butterfly, because it poses a problem the other cases we''ve looked at do not."],["M","Monarchs east of the Rocky Mountains travel as far as three thousand miles each autumn to a few dozen mountain sites in central Mexico — an area smaller than this campus, in total. They arrive at the same groves their ancestors used. And that is the difficulty: no individual butterfly makes the round trip. The generation that flies south is four or five generations removed from the one that left Mexico the previous spring. There is no one to follow and nothing to remember."],["M","So how do they find it? The evidence points to two mechanisms working together. The first is a time-compensated sun compass. The butterfly reads the sun''s position, but since the sun moves across the sky during the day, that reading is useless without a clock — and the clock, it turns out, sits in the antennae, not the brain. Remove the antennae, or simply paint them black, and the animal still flies, but in the wrong direction."],["M","The second mechanism appears to be magnetic. Monarchs tested in flight simulators under artificial magnetic fields reorient when the field is reversed, but only when ultraviolet light is present, which suggests the magnetic sense depends on light-sensitive molecules in the eye."],["M","For Thursday, read the Reppert paper, and be ready to explain why the autumn generation lives eight months while its parents lived five weeks."]]')
insert into questions (id, section, kind, skill, stem, opts, ans, exp, passage_id, no_shuffle, script) values
  ('S01', 'structure', 'plain', 'Frasa partisipial', '____ from Russia in 1867, Alaska did not become a state until 1959.', '["Purchased","It was purchased","Purchasing","The purchase"]', 0, 'Klausa utama sudah lengkap (Alaska did not become). Yang dibutuhkan frasa partisipial pasif tanpa subjek: <em>Purchased…</em> = <em>Because it was purchased…</em> Pilihan dengan subjek+verba membuat dua klausa tanpa konjungsi; <em>Purchasing</em> aktif, padahal Alaska yang dibeli.', null, false, null),
  ('S02', 'structure', 'plain', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'The number of species that inhabit the rain forest ____ still unknown.', '["is","are","being","they are"]', 0, 'Inti subjek adalah <em>The number</em>, bukan <em>species</em>. <em>The number of</em> + jamak selalu tunggal. Bandingkan <em>A number of species are…</em> yang justru jamak.', null, false, null),
  ('S03', 'structure', 'plain', 'Inversi', 'Not until the nineteenth century ____ widely used in the United States.', '["was anesthesia","anesthesia was","anesthesia is","when anesthesia was"]', 0, 'Ungkapan negatif di awal kalimat (<em>Not until, Never, Rarely, Seldom, No sooner</em>) memicu inversi: auxiliary mendahului subjek.', null, false, null),
  ('S04', 'structure', 'plain', 'Struktur paralel', 'The seeds of the sunflower are used for food, oil, and ____.', '["bird feed","they feed birds","to feed birds","feeding of birds"]', 0, 'Rangkaian setelah <em>for</em> harus sejenis: nomina + nomina + nomina — <em>food, oil, and bird feed</em>.', null, false, null),
  ('S05', 'structure', 'plain', 'Klausa relatif tereduksi', 'The instrument ____ to measure atmospheric pressure is the barometer.', '["used","uses","is used","using"]', 0, 'Reduksi dari <em>which is used</em>. Klausa relatif pasif direduksi menjadi past participle. <em>Is used</em> akan membuat kalimat punya dua verba utama.', null, false, null),
  ('S06', 'structure', 'plain', 'Perbandingan', 'The blue whale is ____ animal that has ever lived.', '["the largest","largest","larger than","as large as"]', 0, 'Superlatif wajib memakai <em>the</em>. Penanda <em>that has ever lived</em> menandakan perbandingan terhadap seluruh kelompok, bukan dua hal.', null, false, null),
  ('S07', 'structure', 'plain', 'Apositif', '____, is the capital of Canada.', '["Ottawa, a city in Ontario","Ottawa a city in Ontario","Ottawa is a city in Ontario","In Ontario, Ottawa a city"]', 0, 'Predikat kalimat adalah <em>is the capital</em>, jadi bagian kosong hanya boleh berisi subjek + apositif yang diapit koma.', null, false, null),
  ('S08', 'structure', 'plain', 'Subjek hilang', '____ produces about one-fifth of the world''s oxygen.', '["The Amazon rain forest","In the Amazon rain forest","The Amazon rain forest which","Although the Amazon rain forest"]', 0, 'Kalimat butuh subjek murni. Preposisi di depan (<em>In</em>) atau penambahan <em>which</em>/<em>Although</em> justru menghapus subjek atau membuat klausa menggantung.', null, false, null),
  ('S09', 'structure', 'plain', 'Conditional', 'If the temperature ____ lower, the reaction would have stopped.', '["had been","was","would be","has been"]', 0, 'Hasilnya <em>would have stopped</em> (conditional tipe 3, pengandaian masa lampau), sehingga klausa <em>if</em> harus past perfect: <em>had been</em>.', null, false, null),
  ('S10', 'structure', 'plain', 'Bentuk verba / past perfect', 'By the time the settlers arrived, the disease ____ most of the local population.', '["had killed","killed","has killed","was killing"]', 0, '<em>By the time</em> + simple past menandai dua peristiwa lampau berurutan; yang lebih dulu memakai past perfect.', null, false, null),
  ('S11', 'structure', 'plain', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'Each of the fifty states ____ its own constitution.', '["has","have","having","to have"]', 0, '<em>Each of</em> selalu diikuti verba tunggal, apa pun nomina jamak sesudahnya. Petunjuk tambahan: <em>its</em>, bukan <em>their</em>.', null, false, null),
  ('S12', 'structure', 'plain', 'Inversi', 'So dense ____ that little sunlight reaches the forest floor.', '["is the canopy","the canopy is","the canopy","it is the canopy"]', 0, 'Pola <em>So + adjektiva</em> di awal kalimat memaksa inversi: <em>So dense is the canopy that…</em>', null, false, null),
  ('S13', 'structure', 'plain', 'Gerund setelah preposisi', 'Bees communicate the location of food by ____ a complex dance.', '["performing","perform","performed","to perform"]', 0, 'Setelah preposisi (<em>by, for, without, after</em>) verba selalu berbentuk gerund <em>-ing</em>.', null, false, null),
  ('S14', 'structure', 'plain', 'Pronomina relatif', 'Mercury, ____ is the closest planet to the sun, has almost no atmosphere.', '["which","that","it","what"]', 0, 'Klausa non-restriktif (diapit koma) memakai <em>which</em>, tidak pernah <em>that</em>. <em>It</em> akan menciptakan klausa kedua tanpa konjungsi.', null, false, null),
  ('S15', 'structure', 'plain', 'Inversi', 'Rarely ____ in temperatures below freezing.', '["do mosquitoes survive","mosquitoes survive","mosquitoes do survive","survive mosquitoes"]', 0, 'Adverbia negatif <em>Rarely</em> di posisi awal menuntut inversi dengan <em>do/does/did</em> untuk verba simple present atau past.', null, false, null),
  ('S16', 'structure', 'plain', 'Infinitif tujuan', 'Many desert plants have deep root systems ____ water far below the surface.', '["to reach","reach","reaching to","for reaching"]', 0, 'Untuk menyatakan tujuan, TOEFL menuntut <em>to</em> + verba dasar. <em>Reach</em> polos akan jadi verba utama kedua.', null, false, null),
  ('S17', 'structure', 'plain', 'Klausa nomina', 'Scientists still debate ____ the dinosaurs became extinct.', '["why","why did","the reason why did","because"]', 0, 'Klausa nomina memakai urutan kata pernyataan (subjek + verba), bukan urutan pertanyaan. Jadi <em>why the dinosaurs became</em>, bukan <em>why did…</em>', null, false, null),
  ('S18', 'structure', 'plain', 'Perbandingan paralel', 'The more carefully the data are collected, ____.', '["the more reliable the results","the results are more reliable","more reliable results","the results more reliable are"]', 0, 'Pola <em>The + komparatif …, the + komparatif …</em> harus simetris di kedua sisi.', null, false, null),
  ('S19', 'structure', 'plain', 'Frasa partisipial', '____ across the Great Plains, the pioneers faced severe weather and scarce water.', '["Traveling","They traveled","Traveled","To travel"]', 0, 'Subjek klausa utama (<em>the pioneers</em>) adalah pelaku perjalanan, jadi partisip aktif <em>Traveling</em>. Bentuk pasif <em>Traveled</em> salah karena pionir tidak ''dijalani''.', null, false, null),
  ('S20', 'structure', 'plain', 'Preposisi vs konjungsi', '____ its small size, the shrew must eat almost constantly to survive.', '["Because of","Because","Since","As"]', 0, 'Yang menyusul adalah frasa nomina (<em>its small size</em>), bukan klausa, sehingga butuh preposisi <em>Because of</em>. <em>Because/Since/As</em> menuntut subjek + verba.', null, false, null),
  ('S21', 'structure', 'plain', 'Countable / uncountable', '____ evidence suggests that the site was inhabited for centuries.', '["Considerable","A","Many","Several"]', 0, '<em>Evidence</em> tak terhitung, sehingga tidak bisa memakai <em>a, many, several</em>. Penakar yang cocok: <em>considerable, much, a great deal of</em>.', null, false, null),
  ('S22', 'structure', 'plain', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'There ____ several competing theories about the origin of the moon.', '["are","is","has","being"]', 0, 'Dalam konstruksi <em>there</em>, verba menyesuaikan nomina sesudahnya — di sini <em>theories</em> (jamak).', null, false, null),
  ('S23', 'structure', 'plain', 'Klausa adverbial tereduksi', 'When ____, the alloy becomes considerably harder and more brittle.', '["cooled","it cools","cooling","cools"]', 0, 'Reduksi dari <em>When it is cooled</em>. Karena logam dikenai proses pendinginan (pasif), bentuknya past participle.', null, false, null),
  ('S24', 'structure', 'plain', 'Pronomina posesif', 'The bald eagle builds ____ nest in the tallest trees available.', '["its","it''s","their","it"]', 0, 'Subjek tunggal <em>The bald eagle</em> memerlukan posesif <em>its</em>. <em>It''s</em> adalah singkatan <em>it is</em> — jebakan klasik ITP.', null, false, null),
  ('S25', 'structure', 'plain', 'Urutan kata', 'Only after the invention of the printing press ____ available to ordinary readers.', '["did books become","books became","became books","books did become"]', 0, '<em>Only after</em> di awal kalimat memicu inversi pada klausa utama, bukan pada klausa keterangannya.', null, false, null),
  ('S26', 'structure', 'plain', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'Neither the director nor the actors ____ satisfied with the final scene.', '["were","was","has been","is"]', 0, 'Aturan kedekatan (proximity): dengan <em>neither…nor</em>, verba mengikuti subjek terdekat — di sini <em>the actors</em> (jamak).', null, false, null),
  ('W01', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'The invention of the telephone, radio, and television <u>has revolutionized<sup>A</sup></u> <u>the way<sup>B</sup></u> <u>people<sup>C</sup></u> <u>communicates<sup>D</sup></u> with each other.', '["has revolutionized","the way","people","communicates"]', 3, '<em>People</em> adalah nomina jamak, jadi verbanya <em>communicate</em>. Verba pertama (<em>has revolutionized</em>) benar karena subjeknya <em>The invention</em> — tunggal.', null, true, null),
  ('W02', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'Although <u>both of<sup>A</sup></u> the candidates <u>were qualified<sup>B</sup></u>, <u>neither of them<sup>C</sup></u> <u>were able<sup>D</sup></u> to win a majority.', '["both of","were qualified","neither of them","were able"]', 3, '<em>Neither</em> diperlakukan tunggal: <em>was able</em>. Perhatikan kontras dengan <em>both</em> di awal kalimat yang memang jamak.', null, true, null),
  ('W03', 'structure', 'we', 'Pronomina relatif', 'The scientists <u>which<sup>A</sup></u> <u>discovered<sup>B</sup></u> the vaccine <u>received<sup>C</sup></u> international recognition for <u>their<sup>D</sup></u> work.', '["which","discovered","received","their"]', 0, '<em>Which</em> hanya untuk benda. Untuk orang gunakan <em>who</em> (atau <em>that</em>).', null, true, null),
  ('W04', 'structure', 'we', 'Struktur paralel', 'Hummingbirds are <u>the only<sup>A</sup></u> birds <u>that<sup>B</sup></u> can fly backward, <u>hover<sup>C</sup></u> in midair, and <u>moving<sup>D</sup></u> sideways.', '["the only","that","hover","moving"]', 3, 'Ketiga unsur mengikuti modal <em>can</em>, jadi harus verba dasar: <em>fly, hover, move</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W05', 'structure', 'we', 'Countable / uncountable', 'The <u>amount<sup>A</sup></u> of people <u>attending<sup>B</sup></u> the conference <u>exceeded<sup>C</sup></u> the <u>organizers''<sup>D</sup></u> expectations.', '["amount","attending","exceeded","organizers''"]', 0, '<em>People</em> terhitung, sehingga penakarnya <em>number</em>. <em>Amount</em> hanya untuk yang tak terhitung (<em>amount of water/information</em>).', null, true, null),
  ('W06', 'structure', 'we', 'Preposisi vs konjungsi', '<u>Despite of<sup>A</sup></u> <u>the heavy rain<sup>B</sup></u>, the construction crew <u>continued<sup>C</sup></u> to work <u>through<sup>D</sup></u> the night.', '["Despite of","the heavy rain","continued","through"]', 0, 'Bentuk yang benar adalah <em>Despite</em> atau <em>In spite of</em> — tidak pernah <em>despite of</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W07', 'structure', 'we', 'Perbandingan', 'Sound <u>travels<sup>A</sup></u> <u>more faster<sup>B</sup></u> through water <u>than<sup>C</sup></u> it does <u>through<sup>D</sup></u> air.', '["travels","more faster","than","through"]', 1, 'Komparatif ganda. Adjektiva/adverbia pendek cukup memakai <em>-er</em>: <em>faster</em>, bukan <em>more faster</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W08', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', '<u>Neither<sup>A</sup></u> the manager <u>nor<sup>B</sup></u> the employees <u>was<sup>C</sup></u> informed <u>about<sup>D</sup></u> the change in policy.', '["Neither","nor","was","about"]', 2, 'Aturan kedekatan: subjek terdekat <em>the employees</em> jamak, sehingga verbanya <em>were</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W09', 'structure', 'we', 'Preposisi waktu', 'The professor <u>asked<sup>A</sup></u> the students <u>to hand in<sup>B</sup></u> <u>their<sup>C</sup></u> reports <u>until<sup>D</sup></u> Friday.', '["asked","to hand in","their","until"]', 3, '<em>Until</em> menyatakan durasi sampai suatu titik. Untuk tenggat waktu gunakan <em>by</em>: <em>by Friday</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W10', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', '<u>Many of<sup>A</sup></u> the buildings <u>damaged<sup>B</sup></u> in the earthquake <u>has<sup>C</sup></u> since <u>been repaired<sup>D</sup></u>.', '["Many of","damaged","has","been repaired"]', 2, 'Subjeknya <em>Many of the buildings</em> (jamak). Frasa <em>damaged in the earthquake</em> hanya pewatas, bukan subjek.', null, true, null),
  ('W11', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'She is <u>one of<sup>A</sup></u> the few students <u>who<sup>B</sup></u> <u>has completed<sup>C</sup></u> all the requirements <u>ahead of<sup>D</sup></u> schedule.', '["one of","who","has completed","ahead of"]', 2, 'Dalam pola <em>one of the + jamak + who</em>, <em>who</em> merujuk ke <em>students</em>, sehingga verbanya <em>have completed</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W12', 'structure', 'we', 'Struktur paralel', 'The company <u>announced<sup>A</sup></u> that it would <u>lay off<sup>B</sup></u> workers, <u>close<sup>C</sup></u> two plants, and <u>its headquarters would be relocated<sup>D</sup></u>.', '["announced","lay off","close","its headquarters would be relocated"]', 3, 'Dua unsur pertama adalah verba dasar setelah <em>would</em>. Unsur ketiga harus mengikuti pola yang sama: <em>relocate its headquarters</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W13', 'structure', 'we', 'Pronomina relatif', 'Rice, <u>that<sup>A</sup></u> is <u>the staple food<sup>B</sup></u> of more than half the world, <u>grows<sup>C</sup></u> best in <u>flooded<sup>D</sup></u> fields.', '["that","the staple food","grows","flooded"]', 0, 'Klausa non-restriktif yang diapit koma tidak pernah memakai <em>that</em>; gunakan <em>which</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W14', 'structure', 'we', 'Conditional', 'If he <u>would have studied<sup>A</sup></u> <u>harder<sup>B</sup></u>, he <u>might<sup>C</sup></u> <u>have passed<sup>D</sup></u> the examination.', '["would have studied","harder","might","have passed"]', 0, '<em>Would</em> tidak pernah muncul di klausa <em>if</em>. Conditional tipe 3: <em>If he had studied harder…</em>', null, true, null),
  ('W15', 'structure', 'we', 'Struktur paralel', 'The library is open every day <u>except<sup>A</sup></u> Sunday, <u>when<sup>B</sup></u> it <u>closes<sup>C</sup></u> at noon and <u>reopen<sup>D</sup></u> at four.', '["except","when","closes","reopen"]', 3, 'Dua verba berbagi subjek <em>it</em>, jadi keduanya harus bersufiks <em>-s</em>: <em>closes… reopens</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W16', 'structure', 'we', 'Adjektiva vs adverbia', 'Economists <u>have long argued<sup>A</sup></u> that inflation <u>affects<sup>B</sup></u> the poor <u>more severe<sup>C</sup></u> <u>than<sup>D</sup></u> the wealthy.', '["have long argued","affects","more severe","than"]', 2, 'Yang diterangkan adalah verba <em>affects</em>, sehingga perlu adverbia: <em>more severely</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W17', 'structure', 'we', 'Bentuk jamak', 'The <u>discovery<sup>A</sup></u> of penicillin <u>was<sup>B</sup></u> one of the <u>most important<sup>C</sup></u> medical <u>advance<sup>D</sup></u> of the twentieth century.', '["discovery","was","most important","advance"]', 3, 'Pola <em>one of the + superlatif</em> selalu diikuti nomina jamak: <em>advances</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W18', 'structure', 'we', 'Inversi', '<u>Hardly the meeting had begun<sup>A</sup></u> <u>when<sup>B</sup></u> <u>the fire alarm<sup>C</sup></u> <u>went off<sup>D</sup></u>.', '["Hardly the meeting had begun","when","the fire alarm","went off"]', 0, '<em>Hardly</em> di awal kalimat menuntut inversi: <em>Hardly had the meeting begun when…</em>', null, true, null),
  ('W19', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'A person <u>who exercises<sup>A</sup></u> regularly <u>is likely<sup>B</sup></u> to live <u>longer than<sup>C</sup></u> those who <u>does<sup>D</sup></u> not.', '["who exercises","is likely","longer than","does"]', 3, '<em>Those</em> bersifat jamak, sehingga verbanya <em>do</em>. Bandingkan dengan <em>a person… exercises</em> yang tunggal.', null, true, null),
  ('W20', 'structure', 'we', 'Pola verba', 'The teacher <u>explained us<sup>A</sup></u> <u>the difference<sup>B</sup></u> <u>between<sup>C</sup></u> the two methods <u>very clearly<sup>D</sup></u>.', '["explained us","the difference","between","very clearly"]', 0, '<em>Explain</em> tidak menerima objek tak langsung tanpa preposisi: <em>explained to us</em>. Bandingkan <em>told us</em> yang justru benar.', null, true, null),
  ('W21', 'structure', 'we', 'Inversi', '<u>Not only the drought destroyed<sup>A</sup></u> <u>the crops<sup>B</sup></u>, <u>but<sup>C</sup></u> it <u>also contaminated<sup>D</sup></u> the water supply.', '["Not only the drought destroyed","the crops","but","also contaminated"]', 0, '<em>Not only</em> di awal kalimat memerlukan inversi: <em>Not only did the drought destroy…</em>', null, true, null),
  ('W22', 'structure', 'we', 'Countable / uncountable', '<u>Most of<sup>A</sup></u> the <u>information<sup>B</sup></u> in the report <u>were gathered<sup>C</sup></u> <u>from<sup>D</sup></u> government sources.', '["Most of","information","were gathered","from"]', 2, '<em>Information</em> tak terhitung dan selalu tunggal: <em>was gathered</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W23', 'structure', 'we', 'Struktur paralel', 'The new employees <u>were told<sup>A</sup></u> <u>to arrive<sup>B</sup></u> early, <u>to dress<sup>C</sup></u> formally, and <u>that they should bring<sup>D</sup></u> identification.', '["were told","to arrive","to dress","that they should bring"]', 3, 'Dua unsur pertama berbentuk infinitif, jadi unsur ketiga harus <em>to bring</em>, bukan klausa <em>that</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W24', 'structure', 'we', 'Perbandingan', 'Alaska is <u>the largest<sup>A</sup></u> state in the United States, but it has <u>fewer<sup>B</sup></u> population <u>than<sup>C</sup></u> any other state <u>except<sup>D</sup></u> Wyoming.', '["the largest","fewer","than","except"]', 1, '<em>Population</em> diperlakukan tak terhitung dalam konteks ini: <em>a smaller population</em>. <em>Fewer</em> hanya untuk nomina jamak terhitung.', null, true, null),
  ('W25', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', 'The <u>results<sup>A</sup></u> of the experiment <u>was published<sup>B</sup></u> in a <u>leading<sup>C</sup></u> journal three months <u>later<sup>D</sup></u>.', '["results","was published","leading","later"]', 1, 'Inti subjek <em>results</em> (jamak); <em>of the experiment</em> hanya frasa preposisi yang tidak mengubah jumlah.', null, true, null),
  ('W26', 'structure', 'we', 'Kesesuaian subjek-verba', '<u>Every one<sup>A</sup></u> of the samples <u>were tested<sup>B</sup></u> twice <u>to ensure<sup>C</sup></u> the accuracy of the <u>findings<sup>D</sup></u>.', '["Every one","were tested","to ensure","findings"]', 1, '<em>Every one of</em> selalu tunggal: <em>was tested</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W27', 'structure', 'we', 'Bentuk verba', 'Since the new policy <u>was introduced<sup>A</sup></u>, the number of accidents <u>in the factory<sup>B</sup></u> <u>decreased<sup>C</sup></u> by <u>nearly<sup>D</sup></u> forty percent.', '["was introduced","in the factory","decreased","nearly"]', 2, '<em>Since</em> yang menandai rentang waktu sampai sekarang menuntut present perfect: <em>has decreased</em>.', null, true, null),
  ('W28', 'structure', 'we', 'Artikel', '<u>The gold<sup>A</sup></u> is <u>one of<sup>B</sup></u> the <u>few metals<sup>C</sup></u> that <u>do not corrode<sup>D</sup></u> when exposed to air.', '["The gold","one of","few metals","do not corrode"]', 0, 'Nama zat dalam pengertian umum tidak memakai artikel: <em>Gold is one of…</em>', null, true, null),
  ('W29', 'structure', 'we', 'Kata bilangan', 'The expedition <u>lasted<sup>A</sup></u> <u>three month<sup>B</sup></u> and <u>covered<sup>C</sup></u> more than <u>two thousand<sup>D</sup></u> kilometers.', '["lasted","three month","covered","two thousand"]', 1, 'Nomina terhitung setelah angka harus jamak: <em>three months</em>. <em>Two thousand</em> benar karena angka bulat tidak dijamakkan.', null, true, null),
  ('W30', 'structure', 'we', 'Referensi pronomina', '<u>Each<sup>A</sup></u> of the researchers <u>presented<sup>B</sup></u> <u>their<sup>C</sup></u> findings <u>at<sup>D</sup></u> the annual conference.', '["Each","presented","their","at"]', 2, '<em>Each</em> tunggal, jadi pronomina posesifnya <em>his or her</em>. Pada ITP, pasangan <em>each … their</em> dihitung salah.', null, true, null),
  ('R1a', 'reading', 'reading', 'Gagasan utama', 'What is the main topic of the passage?', '["The adaptations of the saguaro and its role in the desert ecosystem","The decline of desert bird populations in the Southwest","Methods of measuring the age of desert plants","Differences between the Sonoran Desert and other deserts"]', 0, 'Paragraf 1-2 membahas adaptasi, paragraf 3 peran ekologis, paragraf 4 kerentanan. Pilihan lain hanya menyinggung detail kecil. Soal gagasan utama selalu dijawab dengan cakupan seluruh paragraf, bukan satu paragraf.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1b', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'According to the passage, a saguaro grows its first arm at approximately what age?', '["70 years","10 years","3 years","40 years"]', 0, 'Paragraf 1 menyebut cabang pertama muncul sekitar usia tujuh puluh tahun. Angka 10 dan 40 sengaja dipasang sebagai jebakan dari kalimat yang sama.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1c', 'reading', 'reading', 'Kosakata dalam konteks', 'The word "merely" in paragraph 1 is closest in meaning to', '["only","nearly","exactly","barely more than"]', 0, 'Konteksnya menekankan betapa sedikit pertumbuhan dalam sepuluh tahun, sehingga <em>merely</em> = <em>only</em>.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1d', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'The saguaro''s root system is described as', '["shallow but spreading widely","deep and narrow","concentrated in a single taproot","absent in young plants"]', 0, 'Paragraf 2: akar hanya tiga inci di bawah permukaan namun menyebar sejauh tinggi tanamannya.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1e', 'reading', 'reading', 'Inferensi', 'It can be inferred that the pleated structure of the stem serves to', '["let the plant change volume as its water content varies","protect the plant from grazing animals","increase the surface area available for photosynthesis","support the weight of the arms"]', 0, 'Teks menyatakan batang memuai saat menyerap air dan menyusut saat kemarau. Fungsi lipatan disimpulkan dari pasangan <em>expands</em> dan <em>contracts</em>.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1f', 'reading', 'reading', 'Rujukan pronomina', 'The word "them" in paragraph 3 refers to', '["the flowers","bats","cavities","doves"]', 0, 'Kalimatnya membahas bunga yang dikunjungi lebah dan merpati, jadi <em>them</em> merujuk <em>the white flowers</em>.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1g', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail negatif', 'All of the following are mentioned as visiting saguaro flowers EXCEPT', '["woodpeckers","bats","bees","white-winged doves"]', 0, 'Woodpecker disebut membuat lubang sarang, bukan mengunjungi bunga. Soal EXCEPT selesai lebih cepat bila Anda mencoret tiga yang tertulis eksplisit.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1h', 'reading', 'reading', 'Kosakata dalam konteks', 'The word "durable" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to', '["long-lasting","hidden","spacious","warm"]', 0, 'Petunjuknya <em>long after the original occupants have gone</em> — ruang itu bertahan lama.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R1i', 'reading', 'reading', 'Inferensi', 'The passage suggests that the loss of paloverde and mesquite trees is significant because', '["young saguaros cannot survive without their shade","they compete with saguaros for water","they are the main food source for desert bats","they prevent soil erosion around saguaro roots"]', 0, 'Paragraf 4 menghubungkan hilangnya nurse plant dengan menipisnya regenerasi saguaro. Pilihan lain masuk akal secara umum tetapi tidak didukung teks.', 'R1', false, null),
  ('R2a', 'reading', 'reading', 'Gagasan utama', 'The passage is mainly concerned with', '["how the railroad industry created the American time zone system","the engineering problems of nineteenth-century railroads","the passage of the Standard Time Act of 1918","why American towns resisted federal regulation"]', 0, 'Seluruh paragraf bergerak dari masalah waktu lokal ke solusi yang dibuat perusahaan kereta api. Undang-undang 1918 hanya satu kalimat pendukung.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2b', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'According to the passage, local time differences became a serious problem because', '["rail travel was fast enough to make them dangerous","towns refused to set their clocks by the sun","the federal government demanded uniform schedules","clocks of the period were mechanically unreliable"]', 0, 'Paragraf 1-2: selama perjalanan secepat kuda perbedaan itu tak berbahaya; kereta api mengubahnya, bahkan menyebabkan tabrakan.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2c', 'reading', 'reading', 'Kosakata dalam konteks', 'The word "discrepancies" in paragraph 1 is closest in meaning to', '["differences","delays","complaints","distances"]', 0, 'Merujuk ke selisih menit antar kota yang baru disebutkan di kalimat sebelumnya.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2d', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'How many timetables might a traveler in Pittsburgh have had to reconcile?', '["Six","Three","Four","Fifty"]', 0, 'Disebut eksplisit di paragraf 2. Angka tiga dan empat mengacu pada jumlah jam dinding di stasiun, bukan jadwal.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2e', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'The four time zones were established by', '["an association of railway managers","the United States Congress","an international scientific conference","the mayors of major cities"]', 0, 'General Time Convention adalah asosiasi manajer kereta api. Teks menegaskan solusinya bukan dari Congress.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2f', 'reading', 'reading', 'Inferensi', 'The phrase "the day of two noons" suggests that on November 18', '["clocks in many places were set back, so noon occurred twice","two different calendars were in use simultaneously","trains ran on two separate schedules","the sun reached its highest point twice"]', 0, 'Menyetel ulang jam ke zona baru membuat sebagian kota mengulang saat tengah hari. Ini soal inferensi: jawabannya tidak tertulis, tetapi merupakan satu-satunya konsekuensi logis dari penyetelan ulang.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2g', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'Federal recognition of the time zone system came in', '["1918","1883","1870","1930"]', 0, 'Standard Time Act of 1918. Tahun 1883 adalah kesepakatan industri, bukan pengakuan federal — perbedaan inilah yang diuji.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2h', 'reading', 'reading', 'Kosakata dalam konteks', 'The word "compel" in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to', '["force","persuade","invite","reward"]', 0, 'Kontrasnya adalah <em>had no authority</em> — perusahaan tidak bisa memaksa siapa pun.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R2i', 'reading', 'reading', 'Tujuan penulis', 'The author includes the final paragraph primarily to', '["point out that a private standard was adopted without legal force","criticize the railroads for exceeding their authority","explain why some cities kept local time","describe the economic benefits of standard time"]', 0, 'Kalimat penutup — <em>Convenience, not legislation, did the work</em> — menegaskan poin itu. Soal tujuan paragraf dijawab dari kalimat kunci paragraf tersebut, bukan dari keseluruhan teks.', 'R2', false, null),
  ('R3a', 'reading', 'reading', 'Gagasan utama', 'The passage mainly discusses', '["the chemistry, functions, and variations of bioluminescence in the sea","why deep-sea animals have poor eyesight","the difference between animal light and artificial light","how squid defend themselves against predators"]', 0, 'Paragraf bergerak dari kimia, ke fungsi, ke warna, ke sumber bakteri. Pilihan lain hanya detail dari satu paragraf.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3b', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'According to the passage, what proportion of the energy in bioluminescence becomes light?', '["About 95 percent","About 75 percent","About 10 percent","About 200 percent"]', 0, 'Angka 75 persen mengacu pada proporsi hewan yang berpendar, dan 10 persen pada bola lampu pijar. Soal detail berangka menuntut Anda memastikan angka itu melekat pada benda yang tepat.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3c', 'reading', 'reading', 'Kosakata dalam konteks', 'The word "dazzled" in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to', '["temporarily blinded","poisoned","frightened away","trapped"]', 0, 'Konteksnya cumi melepas cairan berpendar lalu kabur, jadi penyerangnya silau sesaat.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3d', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'Counterillumination helps the hatchetfish by', '["preventing it from casting a visible silhouette","attracting prey toward its belly","warning other fish of danger","increasing the light available for hunting"]', 0, 'Organ cahaya di perut menyamai cahaya dari permukaan sehingga pemangsa di bawah tidak melihat bayangan.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3e', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'Most deep-sea bioluminescence is blue-green because', '["those wavelengths travel farthest through seawater","blue-green light requires the least energy to produce","predators cannot see blue-green light","luciferin can only produce that color"]', 0, 'Teks menyebut ini konsekuensi fisika: air laut meneruskan panjang gelombang tersebut paling jauh.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3f', 'reading', 'reading', 'Inferensi', 'It can be inferred that the dragonfish''s red light is useful because', '["its prey cannot see the light being used on them","red light penetrates water farther than blue light","it attracts a wider range of prey species","it produces less heat than blue-green light"]', 0, 'Mata hewan laut dalam hanya peka pada pita sempit biru-hijau, sehingga cahaya merah menjadi sorot lampu pribadi.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3g', 'reading', 'reading', 'Rujukan pronomina', 'The word "them" in paragraph 4 refers to', '["luminous bacteria","fishes and squid","pouches","nutrients"]', 0, 'Inangnya memberi nutrisi kepada koloni bakteri, jadi <em>them</em> = <em>luminous bacteria</em>.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3h', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'The passage indicates that some hosts can control bacterial light by', '["covering it with tissue or turning the organ away","killing part of the colony","changing the color of the light","withholding oxygen from the pouch"]', 0, 'Paragraf 4 menyebut inang dapat menutup dengan lipatan jaringan atau memutarnya agar tidak terlihat.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R3i', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail negatif', 'All of the following functions of bioluminescence are mentioned EXCEPT', '["communicating with mates","attracting prey","avoiding detection","escaping an attacker"]', 0, 'Menarik mangsa (anglerfish), menghindari deteksi (hatchetfish), dan meloloskan diri (cumi) disebut. Komunikasi dengan pasangan tidak pernah disinggung.', 'R3', false, null),
  ('R4a', 'reading', 'reading', 'Gagasan utama', 'What is the main idea of the passage?', '["The Harlem Renaissance was a varied movement shaped by migration and by questions of audience","Langston Hughes was the most influential writer of the 1920s","The Great Migration was caused mainly by wartime industrial jobs","The Depression destroyed African American publishing permanently"]', 0, 'Teks menekankan keragaman gaya, sebab demografis, dan perdebatan tentang audiens. Pilihan lain terlalu sempit atau tidak didukung.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4b', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'According to the passage, why was housing available in Harlem?', '["It had been built for a white middle class that did not fully move in","The city had cleared older buildings for redevelopment","Wartime construction had outpaced demand nationally","Southern migrants arrived with capital to build homes"]', 0, 'Disebut langsung di paragraf 2. Detail semacam ini biasanya muncul sebagai klausa sisipan, bukan kalimat utama.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4c', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'Approximately how many people moved north during the Great Migration described here?', '["1.5 million","1916","One-half million","Fifteen million"]', 0, 'Perhatikan pemisahan angka dan tahun; 1916 adalah awal periode, bukan jumlah orang.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4d', 'reading', 'reading', 'Kosakata dalam konteks', 'The word "coherent" in paragraph 1 is closest in meaning to', '["unified","brief","controversial","forgotten"]', 0, 'Kontras dengan kalimat sebelumnya yang menekankan tidak adanya manifesto atau pemimpin: meski beragam, periode itu diperlakukan sebagai satu kesatuan.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4e', 'reading', 'reading', 'Inferensi', 'The discussion of Cullen, Hughes, and Hurston is included primarily to show that', '["the movement contained sharply different artistic approaches","most Harlem writers had academic training","poetry was the dominant form of the period","the writers collaborated closely with one another"]', 0, 'Kalimat pembuka paragraf 3 menyatakan tidak ada gaya bersama; ketiga nama adalah buktinya.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4f', 'reading', 'reading', 'Detail', 'Langston Hughes was criticized by some contemporaries for', '["portraying working-class life too directly","abandoning American subjects","imitating European poetic forms","refusing support from publishers"]', 0, 'Paragraf 3 menyebut kritik atas penggambaran kehidupan kelas pekerja yang terlalu polos.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4g', 'reading', 'reading', 'Rujukan pronomina', 'The word "it" in the first paragraph, in the phrase "what it was for," refers to', '["the movement","Harlem","the First World War","visual art"]', 0, 'Kalimat itu membahas ketidaksepakatan peserta mengenai tujuan gerakan tersebut.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4h', 'reading', 'reading', 'Inferensi', 'The passage implies that patronage by white supporters was', '["both a source of funding and a cause of concern","universally rejected by Harlem writers","insignificant compared with public funding","the direct cause of the Great Migration"]', 0, 'Paragraf 4 menyebut dukungan finansial sekaligus keraguan apakah karya yang dihasilkan bisa jujur.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('R4i', 'reading', 'reading', 'Organisasi teks', 'How is the passage organized?', '["A definition, then causes, then examples, then an underlying debate","A chronological list of publications","A comparison of two competing movements","An argument followed by counterevidence"]', 0, 'Soal organisasi dijawab dengan memetakan fungsi tiap paragraf, bukan isinya: definisi, sebab, contoh, perdebatan.', 'R4', false, null),
  ('L01', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom: should have', 'What does the woman mean?', '["The man arrived too late to avoid the crowd.","The office opens later than the man thought.","She waited in the same line.","The man should register tomorrow instead."]', 0, '<em>Should have + past participle</em> selalu menyatakan penyesalan atas sesuatu yang tidak dilakukan. Jawabannya menyiratkan waktu kedatangan yang keliru.', null, false, '[["M","I can''t believe how long the line at the registrar''s office was."],["W","You should have gone first thing in the morning."]]'),
  ('L02', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the man mean?', '["He is very eager to attend.","He may not be able to come.","He has other plans that evening.","He does not know where it is held."]', 0, '<em>Wouldn''t miss it for the world</em> adalah penegasan kuat bahwa ia pasti hadir.', null, false, '[["W","Are you going to the lecture on marine biology tonight?"],["M","Wouldn''t miss it for the world."]]'),
  ('L03', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What does the woman imply?', '["She did poorly on the exam.","She enjoys working in the laboratory.","She missed the examination.","The laboratory will be closed."]', 0, '<em>Let''s just say…</em> menandakan jawaban tidak langsung yang menghindari kabar buruk. Konsekuensi yang disebut (lebih banyak waktu di lab) menyiratkan hasilnya jelek.', null, false, '[["M","How did you do on the chemistry midterm?"],["W","Let''s just say I''ll be spending a lot more time in the lab."]]'),
  ('L04', 'listening', 'la', 'Saran', 'What does the man suggest the woman do?', '["Ask the professor about it.","Submit the paper on time.","Avoid speaking with the professor.","Rewrite the paper completely."]', 0, '<em>It wouldn''t hurt to ask</em> = tidak ada ruginya mencoba bertanya.', null, false, '[["W","Do you think Professor Lin would accept my paper a day late?"],["M","It wouldn''t hurt to ask."]]'),
  ('L05', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the woman mean about the apartment?', '["The rent is unusually low.","The rent is higher than average.","It is actually close to campus.","It has already been rented."]', 0, '<em>You can''t beat X</em> = tidak ada yang lebih baik dari X. Di sini soal harga sewa.', null, false, '[["M","This apartment is a bit far from campus."],["W","But you can''t beat the rent."]]'),
  ('L06', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What can be inferred about the man?', '["He has a ticket to the concert.","He was unable to get a ticket.","He sold his ticket to someone.","He decided not to attend."]', 0, 'Ia membeli tiket sebelum kehabisan. Struktur <em>Not until…</em> di sini menandai urutan waktu, bukan penyangkalan.', null, false, '[["W","I heard the concert was sold out."],["M","Not until I''d already bought my ticket."]]'),
  ('L07', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the woman recommend?', '["The subway, without question.","Either option is equally good.","Walking to the museum.","Taking the bus."]', 0, '<em>Hands down</em> = tanpa keraguan sedikit pun.', null, false, '[["M","Should I take the bus or the subway to the museum?"],["W","The subway, hands down."]]'),
  ('L08', 'listening', 'la', 'Restatement', 'What does the man mean?', '["He read only a small portion of it.","He completed all of the reading.","He could not find the book.","The first chapter was easy."]', 0, '<em>Barely</em> bermakna negatif — hampir tidak. Kata ini sering menjadi kunci jawaban di Part A.', null, false, '[["W","Did you finish the reading for tomorrow?"],["M","I barely got through the first chapter."]]'),
  ('L09', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the woman mean?', '["She had not heard about the change.","She scheduled the meeting herself.","She read about it in the newspaper.","She cannot attend on Thursday."]', 0, '<em>That''s news to me</em> = saya baru tahu.', null, false, '[["M","The department meeting has been moved to Thursday."],["W","That''s news to me."]]'),
  ('L10', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What can be inferred about the man?', '["He changed his plans after taking statistics.","He is still majoring in economics.","He failed his statistics course.","He has not chosen any major yet."]', 0, '<em>I was, until…</em> menandakan rencana lama yang berubah karena peristiwa yang disebut sesudahnya.', null, false, '[["W","I thought you were going to major in economics."],["M","I was, until I took a statistics course."]]'),
  ('L11', 'listening', 'la', 'Respons pertanyaan negatif', 'What does the woman mean?', '["The man may open the window.","The window is already open.","She would rather keep it closed.","She will open it herself."]', 0, 'Jawaban <em>Not at all</em> atas <em>Do you mind…</em> berarti izin diberikan. Ini jebakan logika negatif yang sering muncul.', null, false, '[["M","Do you mind if I open the window?"],["W","Not at all."]]'),
  ('L12', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom: persetujuan', 'What does the man mean?', '["He strongly agrees with the woman.","He did not hear the question.","He disagrees with her.","He wants her to repeat herself."]', 0, '<em>You can say that again</em> menyatakan persetujuan penuh, bukan permintaan mengulang.', null, false, '[["W","Professor Ames rarely gives extensions, does she?"],["M","You can say that again."]]'),
  ('L13', 'listening', 'la', 'Saran', 'What does the woman suggest?', '["Visiting the professor during office hours.","Calling again next week.","Emailing the department office.","Meeting a different professor."]', 0, 'Pertanyaan <em>Have you tried…?</em> berfungsi sebagai saran, bukan pertanyaan informasi.', null, false, '[["M","I''ve been trying to reach Dr. Patel all week."],["W","Have you tried her office hours?"]]'),
  ('L14', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the man mean?', '["He was not aware of the new closing time.","He knows the schedule very well.","He wants to eat exactly at seven.","He works in the cafeteria."]', 0, '<em>Since when?</em> mengungkapkan keterkejutan, bukan permintaan tanggal.', null, false, '[["W","The dorm cafeteria closes at seven now."],["M","Since when?"]]'),
  ('L15', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What does the woman imply?', '["She will not be able to join.","She will arrive after midnight.","She has already finished her paper.","The group meets at midnight."]', 0, 'Jawaban tidak langsung berupa alasan hampir selalu berarti penolakan halus.', null, false, '[["M","Are you coming to the study group tonight?"],["W","I have a paper due at midnight."]]'),
  ('L16', 'listening', 'la', 'Restatement', 'What does the man mean?', '["They rarely spend time together.","He does not like the roommate.","They look very similar.","He does not have a roommate."]', 0, '<em>See much of someone</em> berarti sering bertemu, bukan soal penglihatan.', null, false, '[["W","How do you like your new roommate?"],["M","We haven''t seen much of each other."]]'),
  ('L17', 'listening', 'la', 'Saran', 'What does the woman advise the man to do?', '["Consult the advisor before deciding.","Drop the seminar immediately.","Enroll in a different seminar.","Ask other students for advice."]', 0, '<em>If I were you, I''d…</em> adalah pola saran baku dalam Part A.', null, false, '[["M","I''m thinking of dropping the seminar."],["W","If I were you, I''d talk to the advisor first."]]'),
  ('L18', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the man mean?', '["The film was disappointing.","The film was excellent.","He never read the reviews.","The theater was far away."]', 0, '<em>Far from it</em> menyangkal keras pernyataan sebelumnya.', null, false, '[["W","Was the film as good as the reviews said?"],["M","Far from it."]]'),
  ('L19', 'listening', 'la', 'Koreksi informasi', 'What does the woman mean?', '["The deadline has already passed.","The deadline is indeed tomorrow.","Registration opens on Friday.","There is no deadline this term."]', 0, '<em>Actually</em> menandai koreksi. Perhatikan pergeseran kala dari <em>is</em> ke <em>was</em>.', null, false, '[["M","The registration deadline is tomorrow, isn''t it?"],["W","Actually, it was last Friday."]]'),
  ('L20', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the man mean?', '["He is willing to help her.","He is unable to help.","He needs more information.","He is going to the second floor."]', 0, '<em>Say no more</em> = saya sudah paham dan akan membantu. Perhatikan juga <em>I could use…</em> yang berarti membutuhkan.', null, false, '[["W","I could use some help moving these boxes to the third floor."],["M","Say no more."]]'),
  ('L21', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What does the woman imply?', '["Bad weather was probably the reason.","She expected the trip to be popular.","She was never told about the trip.","The forecast turned out to be wrong."]', 0, '<em>Given the forecast</em> menghubungkan pembatalan dengan ramalan cuaca.', null, false, '[["M","Did you hear that the biology field trip was canceled?"],["W","I''m not surprised, given the forecast."]]'),
  ('L22', 'listening', 'la', 'Saran', 'What does the man suggest?', '["Using the library''s reserve copy.","Buying a used edition online.","Sharing the cost with a classmate.","Dropping the course."]', 0, 'Sekali lagi pola <em>Have you checked/tried…?</em> sebagai saran.', null, false, '[["W","This textbook costs almost two hundred dollars."],["M","Have you checked whether the library keeps a copy on reserve?"]]'),
  ('L23', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the woman mean?', '["The man''s appearance is now explained.","She is surprised that he is tired.","He should redo the report.","She also stayed up all night."]', 0, '<em>No wonder</em> = pantas saja; menegaskan sebab yang baru disebut.', null, false, '[["M","I''m exhausted. I stayed up all night finishing the lab report."],["W","No wonder you look so tired."]]'),
  ('L24', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What does the man mean?', '["The woman can find the information herself nearby.","The shuttle has already departed.","He will drive her to the airport.","The schedule was changed recently."]', 0, 'Jawaban tak langsung yang menunjuk sumber informasi. Ia tidak tahu jamnya, tetapi tahu di mana bisa dilihat.', null, false, '[["W","Do you know when the shuttle to the airport leaves?"],["M","There''s a schedule posted by the front desk."]]'),
  ('L25', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What does the woman imply?', '["The information may not be true.","She is transferring next term.","She likes the state university.","She had told him about it earlier."]', 0, 'Pertanyaan balik semacam ini menandakan keraguan atas kabar tersebut.', null, false, '[["M","I heard you''re transferring to the state university."],["W","Where did you hear that?"]]'),
  ('L26', 'listening', 'la', 'Idiom', 'What does the man mean?', '["He experienced the same thing.","He wants to hear more details.","He was not in the room.","He repaired the heating system."]', 0, '<em>Tell me about it</em> adalah ungkapan setuju berdasarkan pengalaman sendiri, bukan permintaan penjelasan.', null, false, '[["W","The seminar room was freezing this morning."],["M","Tell me about it."]]'),
  ('L27', 'listening', 'la', 'Restatement', 'What does the woman mean?', '["She has not visited it but has heard it is good.","She visits the observatory frequently.","The trip there is expensive.","The observatory is closed to students."]', 0, '<em>Neither have I</em> menyatakan kesamaan dalam kalimat negatif; <em>it''s supposed to be</em> berarti menurut kabar orang.', null, false, '[["M","I''ve never been to the observatory on campus."],["W","Neither have I, but it''s supposed to be worth the trip."]]'),
  ('L28', 'listening', 'la', 'Inferensi', 'What does the man mean?', '["The woman is well qualified for it.","She needs more experience first.","The position has already been filled.","He intends to apply as well."]', 0, 'Pertanyaan retoris <em>With your background?</em> berfungsi sebagai pujian atas kelayakannya.', null, false, '[["W","Do you think I should apply for the research assistantship?"],["M","With your background? Absolutely."]]'),
  ('LB1a', 'listening', 'lg', 'Latar percakapan', 'Where does this conversation most likely take place?', '["At a library service desk","In a lecture hall","At a campus bus station","In a bookstore"]', 0, 'Petunjuknya katalog, peminjaman antarperpustakaan, dan denda keterlambatan. Soal latar biasanya dijawab dari dua atau tiga kata kunci di awal.', 'LB1', false, null),
  ('LB1b', 'listening', 'lg', 'Detail', 'Why can''t the woman obtain the book at this library?', '["The library does not own a copy.","The book has been checked out.","The book is restricted to faculty.","The catalog system is down."]', 0, 'Ia menyebut katalog menunjukkan perpustakaan tidak memilikinya.', 'LB1', false, null),
  ('LB1c', 'listening', 'lg', 'Detail', 'How long does an interlibrary loan book normally take to arrive?', '["Seven to ten days","Two days","Twenty minutes","One week exactly"]', 0, 'Dua hari adalah waktu untuk artikel hasil pindai; dua puluh menit adalah lama perjalanan bus. Angka dalam Part B hampir selalu diuji dengan pengecoh dari angka lain di skrip yang sama.', 'LB1', false, null),
  ('LB1d', 'listening', 'lg', 'Detail', 'What does the man suggest the woman do instead?', '["Go to the regional depository in person","Wait for the interlibrary loan","Ask her professor for an extension","Buy the book online"]', 0, 'Karena tenggatnya seminggu, ia menawarkan solusi yang bisa selesai hari itu juga.', 'LB1', false, null),
  ('LB1e', 'listening', 'lg', 'Inferensi', 'Why is the woman concerned about timing?', '["Her research proposal is due in a week.","The library closes early on weekends.","The bus runs infrequently.","Her student ID is about to expire."]', 0, 'Ia menyebut tenggat proposal riset sebagai alasan menolak opsi tujuh sampai sepuluh hari.', 'LB1', false, null),
  ('LB1f', 'listening', 'lg', 'Detail', 'What does the man say about late fees?', '["They are set by the lending library, not by his.","They do not apply to students.","They are charged per week.","They can be waived on request."]', 0, 'Ia membedakan biaya pinjam (gratis untuk mahasiswa) dari denda keterlambatan yang ditentukan perpustakaan pemberi pinjaman.', 'LB1', false, null),
  ('LC1a', 'listening', 'lg', 'Topik utama', 'What is the main topic of the talk?', '["How monarch butterflies navigate to their wintering sites","Why monarch populations are declining","The anatomy of the butterfly antenna","Differences between eastern and western monarchs"]', 0, 'Kalimat pembuka menyebut unit navigasi hewan, dan seluruh ceramah membahas dua mekanisme penunjuk arah.', 'LC1', false, null),
  ('LC1b', 'listening', 'lg', 'Inferensi', 'Why does the professor consider the monarch a special problem?', '["No individual butterfly has made the journey before.","The butterflies travel farther than any other insect.","Their destination changes every year.","They migrate only at night."]', 0, 'Generasi yang terbang ke selatan terpisah empat atau lima generasi dari yang meninggalkan Meksiko, sehingga tidak mungkin belajar atau mengingat rute.', 'LC1', false, null),
  ('LC1c', 'listening', 'lg', 'Detail', 'According to the professor, the butterfly''s internal clock is located in', '["the antennae","the brain","the eyes","the wings"]', 0, 'Ia menegaskan jam itu berada di antena, bukan otak — persis titik yang ditandai dengan <em>it turns out</em>, penanda informasi yang akan diujikan.', 'LC1', false, null),
  ('LC1d', 'listening', 'lg', 'Detail', 'What happens when a monarch''s antennae are painted black?', '["It continues to fly but in the wrong direction.","It becomes unable to fly at all.","It stops responding to magnetic fields.","It reverses its migration completely."]', 0, 'Disebut eksplisit: hewan tetap terbang tetapi arahnya keliru.', 'LC1', false, null),
  ('LC1e', 'listening', 'lg', 'Detail', 'The magnetic response of monarchs depends on the presence of', '["ultraviolet light","warm temperatures","other butterflies nearby","a visible horizon"]', 0, 'Reorientasi hanya terjadi ketika ada sinar ultraviolet, sehingga diduga melibatkan molekul peka cahaya di mata.', 'LC1', false, null),
  ('LC1f', 'listening', 'lg', 'Tugas / arahan', 'What are students asked to prepare for the next class?', '["A reading and an explanation of the generations'' different lifespans","A laboratory report on flight simulators","A field observation of local butterflies","A summary of the entire unit"]', 0, 'Instruksi di akhir ceramah hampir selalu menjadi satu butir soal Part C. Biasakan menandai kalimat setelah <em>For Thursday…</em> atau <em>Before next class…</em>', 'LC1', false, null)
